Error [E2511]: `+` isn't defined between `F32x4` and `F64x2`
  --> tests/ui/math_operator_mismatch.jet:5:18
    |
  5 |     bad :: F32x4{v + w}
    |                  ^^^^^
 Why: Built-in lane and linalg operators keep fixed shapes: one lane/vector type on both sides, or a matrix and its matching vector; any other pair needs an operator hook
 Fix: Match the operand types (`T.splat(x)` lifts a scalar into every lane), call a named method like `.dot()`/`.matmul()`, or implement the operator's hook trait on your own type for this pair
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2511
